  "result": {
    "summary": "All 8 named acceptance tests plus the base gate ran green in this worktree (41/41 pass). Verified independently: migration against the repo's real .orchestrator/memory files produces exactly the counts documented in 01-memory-store.md (235 records: 83 decisions, 103 gotchas, 1 reference, 46 architecture, 2 model notes). Markdown files are untouched by migrate (asserted in test and confirmed by design \u2014 add() only writes SQLite). Rebuild reversibility, FTS5 external-content triggers keeping records_fts in sync, LIKE fallback with metadata warning, goal-label/source_tasks extraction with KeyError/FileNotFoundError-only bus lookups, architecture.md's header-date-applies-to-bullets parsing, and the reference kind mapping all match the folded-in spec-review requirements and are exercised by tests. .gitignore and install.py IGNORE_LINES both cover index.sqlite and its wal/shm variants. All SQL is parameterized (including the FTS MATCH and json_each membership filters); task ids used to build task-json paths are constrained by a strict T-\\d{4} regex, so no injection or traversal surface. No secrets written, no bare excepts. Scope matches the diff exactly.",
